window.bookSummaryJSON = "<i><b>I unraveled Miriam's world with a single eviction notice.<br>She never saw it coming.</b></i><br><br>Desperate and out of options, she found my carefully crafted snare, an ad for room and board<br>in exchange for help with my college thesis. <br><br>To her, the opportunity was heaven-sent. To me, it was just another ritual for my coven,<br>The 12 Knights of Adika. She was one of many blind, Christian lambs I'd drawn into a world<br>never to be escaped.<br><br>But as I engaged in my facade of philosophical debates, her unwavering faith<br>clashed with my cold atheism, sparking a dangerous fascination. Her remarkable defiance<br>and unyielding spirit against sound logic awakened an obsession in me. I called it... The Miriam Obsession.<br><br>For the first time ever, I invoked the order's right to keep an offering for myself, a privilege allowed only once. <br>I wanted Miriam to be <i>my </i>lamb. And <i>no </i>other.<br><br>But the 12 Knights betrayed me. And now every ounce of my honed malevolence dug in<br>to defend what was rightfully mine. Mine to keep, mine to possess. While I hid her from<br>the order's grasp, I did exactly that. I feasted on her decadent purity. I ruthlessly ruined her,<br>stripping away her faith with every erotic, sadistic game I played.<br><br>And yet...what's that saying... <i>\"It all went to hell in a handbasket\"</i> in one of my games.<br>My little lamb made a move I never saw coming. A play that changed everything. <br><br><i><b>Now...The 12 Knights of Adika are no longer her greatest threat. I am.</b></i>"; 
